  "provider_query": "Public Telegram web preview of the official Telegram channel",
  "answer": "The official Telegram channel is **@telegram** (“Telegram News”). Its public web preview (no login) is at **https://t.me/s/telegram**.\n\n1. **Public web preview (official channel)** — https://t.me/s/telegram — latest posts as HTML; description: “The official Telegram on Telegram.” [web:13]\n2. **Channel link** — https://t.me/telegram — standard public channel URL (opens preview or the app). [web:13]\n3. **How the preview works** — every public channel at `t.me/name` has a no-login preview at `t.me/s/name` with recent posts (text, media, views, timestamps). [web:2]\n4. **Paging older posts** — append `?before=<post-id>` (example: https://t.me/s/telegram?before=461). [web:13]\n5. **Single post** — `https://t.me/s/telegram/<id>` (example: https://t.me/s/telegram/81). [web:16]\n6. **What the preview shows** — message text, view counts, forward headers, media URLs, and approximate subscriber count; not full comment threads or deleted posts. [web:2]\n7. **Official site (announcements)** — Telegram says official announcements are only at telegram.org; other sites claiming that role are likely scams. [web:16]\n8. **Logged-in web client (not the public preview)** — https://web.telegram.org — full app in the browser; requires login. [web:10]\n\n**Direct link:** [https://t.me/s/telegram](https://t.me/s/telegram)",
